WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.640
Imagine an alien civilization

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.960
is looking up at the night sky

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.400
scanning the heavens,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.120
trying to detect signs of life.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.520
We as a species have been sending
out radio signals for about 100 years

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.960
and we have followed that up
with television signals.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.680
Those signals have gone into space
and travelled at the speed of light

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.600
and by now have reached
hundreds of stars

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.400
and hundreds of planets around them.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.920
So if there was an alien civilization
in that distance

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.440
and they were pointing their
detectors roughly in our direction

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.400
they would have heard
the first BBC broadcasts,

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.120
and by now they would have seen
many, many years of Coronation Street

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.640
and have a rough idea
of how our humanity works.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.880
Some very prominent scientists
think it's quite silly

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.960
that we're sharing quite so much
about ourselves to the galaxy.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.400
Aliens may not be very kind

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.520
and maybe we shouldn't
be giving away our position

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.400
and our entertainment choices.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.720
Maybe we should all just collectively

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.800
stop advertising ourselves
to the galaxy.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.560
So imagine
that same alien civilization

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.520
looking at the night sky

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.520
but now there are no radio signals,
no television signals,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.800
just 300 billion beautiful white
lights, quietly shining away.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.200
But it is the white light,
seemingly so fundamental and pure,

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.120
that holds the key
to unlocking the secrets

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.320
of all those planets
around all those stars.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.120
White light is only pure
until you crack it open.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.040
With a prism or a drop of water,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.280
white light shows
what really is within it.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.400
The rainbow. And the rainbow isn't
just made up of seven colours.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.040
With a powerful enough prism

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.160
you can get all of the reds
and all of the violets,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.880
all of the infinite colours
between them and beyond them,

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.360
in the infrared and the ultraviolet.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.720
So if that alien civilization pointed
their very expensive prism at our sun

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.080
they'll be able to see
our sun's rainbow.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.080
And if they were very patient
and looked carefully

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.360
they would notice that every year

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.040
a few new shadows would appear
and then disappear.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.520
And they would appear and disappear.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.920
And those shadows are caused
by the molecules in our atmosphere.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.240
And they will be able to look at
those shadows in the rainbow

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.080
and know that we have
an extremely lively planet.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.040
That we have vast inhabited oceans,
that we're oxygen reliant lifeforms,

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.560
that we have at least one
technological species

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.880
and also that we pollute a lot.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.920
The Earth has a living atmosphere -

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.520
we call that a biosphere -

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.200
and that biosphere is a planet-sized,
unintentional message

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.440
to any aliens out there
that care to listen.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.640
It tells the story of who lives on
this planet and what we do with it.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.760
So we could stop
sending messages into space

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.280
but even if we do go quiet,
they can still tell we're here.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.760
It's the galactic equivalent
of thinking "I'm invisible now".

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.960
Well we can already look
at some alien atmospheres,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.120
although we can't quite look
at a full terrestrial atmosphere yet,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.000
but we're very close.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.000
At MIT, I develop the tools
to try to decipher

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.720
these potential alien biospheres.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.240
Those tools are how I will be
listening in to alien messages.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.520
And of course I would love to receive

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.640
the alien version of The Simpsons
coming down from the heavens.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.240
Until then I will be looking
for the signs of life

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:12.200
that the aliens
didn't even mean to create.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:20.260
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

